# Ignore everything by default.
*

# Include the following.
!LICENSE.md
!README.md
!dist/**
!package.json
!src/**/*.ts

# Ship the source alongside dist so the emitted declaration maps (.d.ts.map) and source maps (.js.map) resolve to readable TypeScript - "go to definition" and
# debugger step-into land on the real source rather than on generated output. The allow rule names TypeScript specifically, because TypeScript is the only thing a
# shipped map can point at, so whatever else lands under src stays out by construction rather than by a rule someone has to remember to add. The dev-only source
# shapes the build keeps out of dist are then re-ignored below, mirroring tsconfig.build.json's exclusions. `npm run lint:pack` is the arbiter of the result.
src/**/*.fixtures.ts
src/**/*.helpers.ts
src/**/*.test.ts
src/**/*.types.test.ts
src/**/*.types.ts
src/internal/**
